      "message": "This logic looks duplicated with what you wrote for `publishFrusOnBus`,\n\nis there any chance we can stack a patch below this one to implement `publishAllFrus` to call `publishFrusOnBus` in a loop (for each bus) or something like that?\n\n\nThere are some subtle differences like that `publishAllFrus` clears the interface maps first and then publishes and `publishFrusOnBus` only clears for one bus.\n\nBut if we make sure that `publishFrusOnBus` only tries to clear (and does not throw on failing to do so) then it might be safe to call it in a loop from `publishAllFrus` even if the maps are already cleared beforehand.\n\n\nIs there anything preventing us from doing it like that and implementing `ReScan` in terms of multiple (internal) calls to the `ReScanBus` implementation?\n\nThat way you would only need to implement your feature in a single function and we can avoid having to manually test two different code paths.",
